# Review ownership. The rules these encode are written out in
# docs/governance/review-charter.md; this file is how GitHub enforces them.
#
# There is no catch-all line on purpose. The approval counts the charter
# asks for (s2) are checked by scripts/quorum_check.py against
# .github/quorum-roster.toml, and the reviews a change still needs are
# requested from the roster by the hourly sweep, so a catch-all here would
# only route every pull request to every core reviewer at once.
#
# Later entries win. The entries below are the paths the charter protects
# (s4). A line that names several people is satisfied by any one of them:
# that is how GitHub reads it and how scripts/quorum_check.py counts it.

# Paths the charter protects (s4): these need a code owner's approval in
# addition to the usual quorum. On most of them the owner is the maintainer.
/.github/ @chernistry
# The core package and the adapters are shared with the core reviewers: any
# one of the people named supplies the owner's approval. The four
# subpackages listed right after core/ are the exception and stay with the
# maintainer; they come later in the file, so they win.
/src/bernstein/core/ @chernistry @vaibhav8a @thegoodengineer @tenequm @Phoenix1504e @Chirag6722
/src/bernstein/core/security/ @chernistry
/src/bernstein/core/identity/ @chernistry
/src/bernstein/core/sandbox/ @chernistry
